AstrOsRandomEffects
===================

Pure, native-testable decisions for the random span script commands (types 6
and 7, .docs/protocol.md § C): the servo move rule, gap draws, the travel-time
gap stretch, and RandomSpanTable, the fixed-capacity table of active spans.
The RNG is injected (Rand32), so native tests script or seed it; the
random-effects task in src/main.cpp (T-009) owns the table and passes
esp_random. Parsing lives in AstrOsAnimationCommands (RandomCommands.hpp).

Purity rule
-----------

This library is unit-tested on the native host under [env:test], so it
must not include any of:

    freertos/*, esp_*, driver/*, nvs_*, sdmmc_*, esp_vfs*, esp_now*, esp_wifi*

Enforced by the CI purity guard in .github/workflows/pr-validation.yml.

Error-channel convention
------------------------

No logging and no exceptions. RandomSpanTable::Start returns false when the
table is full or the gaps break § C; the MIXED caller logs at the boundary.
RandomSpanTable is not thread-safe: the caller holds one lock around every
call (T-009: randomTableMutex).
